{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25146680",
      "title": "Getting Started with Fetching Data",
      "lectureOrder": 77,
      "videoOrder": 72,
      "sourceHash": "6f6d1fb341c8c14f8d57421c9bd14fdd61efc9af067c2d77c31426acedbb2d4b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.19,
          "end": 5.3,
          "en": "So let's now make sure that we load the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.3,
          "end": 9.02,
          "en": "we store here on Firebase into our application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.02,
          "end": 10.59,
          "en": "into our website here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.59,
          "end": 13.9,
          "en": "when we load this starting page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.9,
          "end": 16.8,
          "en": "Because at the moment here in the All Meetups page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.8,
          "end": 18.6,
          "en": "we're still using this dummy data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.6,
          "end": 21.02,
          "en": "And that's of course not the goal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.02,
          "end": 24.87,
          "en": "Now to load data from our back and from our API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.87,
          "end": 28.18,
          "en": "we need to send a HTTP request again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.18,
          "end": 32.27,
          "en": "just as we send one when we store data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.27,
          "end": 34.61,
          "en": "So in the AllMeetups js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.61,
          "end": 36.95,
          "en": "in the \"AllMeetups Page\" component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.95,
          "end": 38.56,
          "en": "we want to send the request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.56,
          "end": 42.22,
          "en": "The question is, when do we wanna to send the request?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.22,
          "end": 46.43,
          "en": "And the answer is whenever this component is being rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.43,
          "end": 49.163,
          "en": "So whenever we visit this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.06,
          "end": 53.3,
          "en": "So what you could do, what could be your first idea,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.3,
          "end": 56.69,
          "en": "is that directly in this component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.69,
          "end": 59.81,
          "en": "before we returned to JSX code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.81,
          "end": 62.37,
          "en": "we can \"fetch\" our data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.37,
          "end": 66.94,
          "en": "We can use the same URL as we used for storing the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.94,
          "end": 68.35,
          "en": "Since you want to \"fetch\" data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.35,
          "end": 70.523,
          "en": "from the same API and node,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.51,
          "end": 74.263,
          "en": "and hence, we can use the same URL here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.82,
          "end": 79.25,
          "en": "Now, we don't need to configure this request here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.25,
          "end": 81.5,
          "en": "with this second argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.5,
          "end": 85.9,
          "en": "because the default is that a \"get\" request is sent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.9,
          "end": 89.09,
          "en": "and that's exactly the kind of request we need here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.09,
          "end": 92.84,
          "en": "We want to send a request to get our data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.84,
          "end": 95.2,
          "en": "So we can call \"\"fetch\"\" just like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.2,
          "end": 98,
          "en": "And this will \"fetch\" this data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98,
          "end": 101.43,
          "en": "But now, unlike as with the \"POST\" request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.43,
          "end": 105.03999999999999,
          "en": "when we sent data, now, when we get data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.03999999999999,
          "end": 109.11,
          "en": "we are definitely also interested in the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.11,
          "end": 111.78,
          "en": "Now since \"fetch\" returns a promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.78,
          "end": 115.46000000000001,
          "en": "we can of course use the \"then\" method here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.46000000000001,
          "end": 120.46,
          "en": "and change this after \"then\" to handle this response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.62,
          "end": 122.96,
          "en": "So we pass an anonymous function to \"then\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.96,
          "end": 125.19,
          "en": "and here we'll get the response object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.19,
          "end": 127.31,
          "en": "as an argument automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.31,
          "end": 129.9,
          "en": "because that's how the \"\"fetch\"\" function works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.9,
          "end": 133.61,
          "en": "It returns a promise, which resolves to the actual response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.61,
          "end": 134.993,
          "en": "at some point in time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.85,
          "end": 138.68,
          "en": "Now, from that response, we want to read the body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 138.68,
          "end": 140.34,
          "en": "We want to read the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.34,
          "end": 143.23,
          "en": "and we can do that with the \"json\" method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.23,
          "end": 144.81,
          "en": "That's a method which exists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.81,
          "end": 147.51,
          "en": "on this response object out of the box.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.51,
          "end": 148.9,
          "en": "And this will give us access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.9,
          "end": 152.8,
          "en": "to that data automatically converted from \"json\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.8,
          "end": 155.41,
          "en": "to a plain JavaScript object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.41,
          "end": 156.577,
          "en": "But here's a gotcha,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 156.577,
          "end": 160.2,
          "en": "\"json\" will actually return a promise as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.2,
          "end": 163.52,
          "en": "So we also need to wait for this promise to resolve.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 163.52,
          "end": 167.32,
          "en": "So I actually will return \"response,Json\" here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 167.32,
          "end": 169.48,
          "en": "and add another \"then\" block,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 169.48,
          "end": 172.39,
          "en": "where we then get the actual data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 172.39,
          "end": 174.197,
          "en": "And it's now in this second",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.197,
          "end": 178.75,
          "en": "\"then\" block where we can work on that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.75,
          "end": 181.32,
          "en": "We could also add error handling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 181.32,
          "end": 183.74,
          "en": "and we do that in the complete guide course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 183.74,
          "end": 185.94,
          "en": "But for the moment here, let's focus",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 185.94,
          "end": 189.193,
          "en": "on just getting that data and using that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.03,
          "end": 193.15,
          "en": "So here in this \"then\" block, we get the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.15,
          "end": 195.96,
          "en": "What do we want to do with this data now?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 195.96,
          "end": 198.57999999999998,
          "en": "In the end, we want to extract an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198.57999999999998,
          "end": 202.53,
          "en": "of meetups from that response data and pass that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 202.53,
          "end": 205.913,
          "en": "as a value to the meetups prop on the meetup list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 206.75,
          "end": 208.97,
          "en": "Now we'll have a problem here though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 208.97,
          "end": 211.07,
          "en": "Since \"\"fetch\"\" returns a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 211.07,
          "end": 215.94,
          "en": "and we're in this promise chain, JavaScript does not wait",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 215.94,
          "end": 220.57,
          "en": "for this promise to complete before we return here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 220.57,
          "end": 223.75,
          "en": "Now you could think that we can use \"async await\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 223.75,
          "end": 226.42000000000002,
          "en": "here to wait until this is done,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 226.42000000000002,
          "end": 229.06,
          "en": "but that would be bad because that would mean",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 229.06,
          "end": 233.51,
          "en": "that the entire component function now returns a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 233.51,
          "end": 236.13,
          "en": "because that's what the \"async\" keyword does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 236.13,
          "end": 237.57999999999998,
          "en": "It converts this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 237.57999999999998,
          "end": 239.85,
          "en": "to a function that returns a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 239.85,
          "end": 243.33,
          "en": "and that then no longer qualifies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 243.33,
          "end": 245.97,
          "en": "as a valid React component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 245.97,
          "end": 249.94,
          "en": "because React component functions must be synchronous",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 249.94,
          "end": 252.08,
          "en": "and must not return a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 252.08,
          "end": 256.35,
          "en": "but instead they have to directly return JSX.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 256.35,
          "end": 259.35,
          "en": "So we can't use \"async, await\" weight here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 259.35,
          "end": 263.09,
          "en": "Hence we can't defer returning a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 263.09,
          "end": 265.27,
          "en": "until we have a response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 265.27,
          "end": 268.35,
          "en": "Instead, what we need to do is we need to return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 268.35,
          "end": 272.86,
          "en": "some temporary JSX code, for example, a loading spinner",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 272.86,
          "end": 274.46,
          "en": "or something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 274.46,
          "end": 277.12,
          "en": "And then once we have the response, we want to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 277.12,
          "end": 280.18,
          "en": "update the returned JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 280.18,
          "end": 283.79,
          "en": "And how do we change what's visible on the screen?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 283.79,
          "end": 285,
          "en": "With \"state\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 285,
          "end": 288.15,
          "en": "That's what we learned earlier already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 288.15,
          "end": 292.72,
          "en": "We can use \"state\" to change what's displayed on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 292.72,
          "end": 295.47,
          "en": "when certain conditions change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 295.47,
          "end": 298.73,
          "en": "Before we did that, when the user clicked a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 298.73,
          "end": 301.35,
          "en": "and we wanted to show an overlay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 301.35,
          "end": 304.893,
          "en": "Now I want to change the \"state\" once we have response data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 305.75,
          "end": 309.56,
          "en": "So for that here in this AllMeetups JS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 309.56,
          "end": 313.61,
          "en": "we can import \"useState\" from React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 313.61,
          "end": 316.12,
          "en": "So this \"useState\" hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 316.12,
          "end": 319.907,
          "en": "And then register some state here with \"useState\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 321.4,
          "end": 324.693,
          "en": "And here we could, for example, set up some loading state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 325.66,
          "end": 329.53,
          "en": "So name the constant \"loading\", or \"isLoading\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 329.53,
          "end": 333.61,
          "en": "and add a \"setIsloading\" state updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 333.61,
          "end": 335.97,
          "en": "Because you learned that \"useState\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 335.97,
          "end": 339.49,
          "en": "always returns an array with exactly two elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 339.49,
          "end": 342.93,
          "en": "where the first element is the current state snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 342.93,
          "end": 347.27,
          "en": "And the second element is a function for updating the state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 347.27,
          "end": 350.65999999999997,
          "en": "And when we have data we want to set \"isLoading\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 350.65999999999997,
          "end": 353.85,
          "en": "to \"false\" again, because we're not loading anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 353.85,
          "end": 356.77,
          "en": "but actually the initial state here should be \"true\",",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 356.77,
          "end": 358.09000000000003,
          "en": "not \"false\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 358.09000000000003,
          "end": 360.24,
          "en": "So we start in a loading state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 360.24,
          "end": 364.52,
          "en": "and then we set it to false, once we have the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 364.52,
          "end": 369.52,
          "en": "And then with that, we could check if we are loading here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 369.84,
          "end": 373.31,
          "en": "in the component function, before we return, I check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 373.31,
          "end": 376.45,
          "en": "if we are loading, and if we are,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 376.45,
          "end": 381.09,
          "en": "then I want to return another piece of JSX code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 381.09,
          "end": 382.67,
          "en": "where I, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 382.67,
          "end": 386.32,
          "en": "have a section with a paragraph where I say, \"loading\",",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 386.32,
          "end": 387.623,
          "en": "something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 388.48,
          "end": 391.81,
          "en": "So that's my fallback content, which I want to return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 391.81,
          "end": 394.57,
          "en": "in this component whilst we are loading.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 394.57,
          "end": 397.49,
          "en": "And we only return the actual meetup list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 397.49,
          "end": 400.373,
          "en": "if we're done loading, so if we have the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 401.3,
          "end": 402.5,
          "en": "But speaking of that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 402.5,
          "end": 405.09000000000003,
          "en": "there we're missing an important point.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 405.09000000000003,
          "end": 407.83,
          "en": "At the moment, we're just managing the loading state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 407.83,
          "end": 409.27,
          "en": "We're not doing anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 409.27,
